title: The dark cellar
story: fernhill
continues: key
description: The tarnished key's door, and the room behind it that cannot be
  seen without the lamp from the landing.

---

> north
[OK: contains "Entrance Hall"]

> north
[OK: contains "Cellar Stairs"]
[OK: contains "An oil lamp sits in a wall niche"]

> take the oil lamp
[OK: contains "Taken"]
[STATE: true, player.inventory contains lamp]

# `lockable with the tarnished key` — and unlike the fuse and the deed box,
# `unlock` takes its instrument naturally because the phrasing names it.
> unlock the cellar door with the tarnished key
[OK: contains "You unlock the cellar door with the tarnished key"]

# `after opening it, once / award unsealed` — 5 points, taking the total to 10
# and triggering the Guest of the House promotion line.
> open the cellar door
[OK: contains "You open the cellar door"]
[OK: contains "The house has stopped listening for your footsteps"]

# PLATFORM TEXT LEAK, asserted as it behaves. The stdlib default for entering
# an unlit room is Dungeo's grue line, in a story with no grues, no Dungeo, and
# a 1920s English country-house register. An author gets this sentence for free
# and has no obvious place to override it.
> down
[OK: contains "It is pitch dark. You are likely to be eaten by a grue"]
[STATE: true, player.location = Cellar]

# The room's `on every turn / phrase cellar-drip` runs in the dark — the player
# cannot see but can hear.
> look
[OK: contains "It's pitch dark, and you can't see a thing"]
[OK: contains "The dark keeps its own time"]

# `light-source, switchable`. Switching it on re-describes the room in the
# same turn, and `on every turn while the oil lamp is lit, once` fires.
> switch on the oil lamp
[OK: contains "The oil lamp switches on, banishing the darkness"]
[OK: contains "Brick vaults run off into the dark"]
[OK: contains "You can see a crowbar here"]
[OK: contains "Something small skitters away from your lamplight and is gone"]

# `, once` — the startle does not repeat.
> look
[OK: contains "Brick vaults run off into the dark"]
[OK: not contains "Something small skitters away"]

> take the crowbar
[OK: contains "Taken"]
[STATE: true, player.inventory contains crowbar]

# found (5) + unsealed (5).
> score
[OK: contains "You have scored 10 out of 50"]
